# Line-ending policy for the command entry layer.
#
# The Makefile must keep LF endings on EVERY platform. On a Windows checkout
# with core.autocrlf=true, Git rewrites text files to CRLF; GNU Make then treats
# the trailing CR as part of the target and shell-command names (e.g. `help\r`),
# which breaks target resolution and recipe execution. Pinning this one file to
# LF keeps `make check` byte-identical on Windows and on Linux CI.
#
# Deliberately narrow: no `* text=auto`, to avoid a repo-wide renormalisation.
# This file itself stays LF too, so the rules remain diff-stable on Windows.
#
# Frozen eval datasets (routing + approval policy) are sha256-pinned.
# A Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true would rewrite them to CRLF
# and fail manifest verification. Pin the directory to LF.
.gitattributes text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf
tests/data/** text eol=lf
